    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d912">

                <pb facs="1048" n="854" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv02/pg854"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Department of the Army Files: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 912<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Representative on the Allied
                        Commission on Reparations</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Pauley</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Delegation to the Allied Commission on
                        Reparations</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">urgent</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Babelsberg</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-22">July 22 [<hi rendition="#italic">21?</hi>],
                            1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Victory</hi> 190. Reference your cable of July
                        18.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d912-f1"/> (To Sproul from Deane from Pauley for
                    Abramovitz and Bergson) Please send at once the following additional information
                        <hi rendition="#italic">one</hi> approximate estimate of value of industrial
                    and mining output in Russian zone in 1938 <hi rendition="#italic">two</hi>
                    approximate estimated value of agricultural production in the same zone <hi
                        rendition="#italic">three</hi> approximate percentage that each of the above
                    constitute of total pre-war German production <hi rendition="#italic">four</hi>
                    approximate percentage of total German industrial and mining production that
                    came from area east of Oder Neisse river[s] in 1939. Above information needed
                    urgently.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
